  "_commit": {
    "id": "08dc4565d85caf2db6f19bbfb0d53d054720b376",
    "author": "Buyan Khurelbaatar <158336401+buyan-kh@users.noreply.github.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Add the Z suffix to GeoParquet geometry types for 3D data\n\nwriteGeoParquet() never added the GeoParquet spec's required \" Z\"\nsuffix (e.g. \"Point Z\") to a 3D geometry's type in the written file's\ngeo metadata, so readers like GDAL/OGR had no way to know a column had\na Z coordinate without scanning every geometry.\n\n.geometryTypeToGeoParquet() now classifies each geometry individually\n(by type and whether it carries a Z coordinate, via a new .sfcHasZ()\nhelper) before deduplicating, so a column mixing 3D and 2D geometries\nof the same base type (e.g. after writeGeoParquet(..., append = TRUE))\ncorrectly lists both \"Point Z\" and \"Point\". Covers both normal writes\nand append = TRUE.\n\nFixes #1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Buyan Khurelbaatar <158336401+buyan-kh@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
    "time": 1794459148
  },
